[ system ]
    You decide which of these people in Skyrim, if any, would write a letter to {{ player }} now, unprompted. Use what their profiles, memories and talks with {{ player }} say. Your whole answer is one compact JSON object.
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    {% for c in candidates %}
    ## {{ c.number }}. {{ c.name }}, {{ c.place }}
    {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", c.UUID) }}
    {% if c.never_met %}Has never met {{ player }}.{% endif %}
    {% if c.days_since_seen == 0 %}Dealt with {{ player }} earlier today.{% else if c.days_since_seen == 1 %}Last dealt with {{ player }} a day ago.{% else if c.days_since_seen > 1 %}Last dealt with {{ player }} {{ c.days_since_seen }} days ago.{% endif %}
    {% if c.dialogue and length(c.dialogue) > 0 %}
    The last time they spoke:
    {% for line in c.dialogue -%}
    {{ line.speaker }}: {{ line.text }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if c.memories and length(c.memories) > 0 %}
    What {{ c.name }} remembers of {{ player }}:
    {% for memory in c.memories -%}
    - {{ memory }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    {% endfor %}
    {{ player }} is in {{ player_place }} now. Use this location to judge whether they could talk in person. Ground each candidate's knowledge of {{ player }}'s whereabouts in their conversations and memories.

    People write when they have a reason: news of their own, something unfinished with {{ player }}, gratitude, worry, a favour to ask, a grudge, or missing someone they are close to. A personal or practical connection can support a letter: shared work or business is enough for professional correspondence. Ground personal familiarity in their established relationship and shared experiences. A first contact needs a reason to approach {{ player }} specifically. Someone close enough to walk over and talk to {{ player }} prefers speaking in person.

    Pick the person with the strongest reason, by their number, or 0 if nobody has one, with the reason in a few words: {"pick": <number>, "why": "<reason>"}
[ end user ]
